WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.953
Why keep a tool running all night for one morning report?

00:00:03.953 --> 00:00:06.309
With SlimFaas, idle agent tools can sleep.

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:09.006
Keep your existing HTTP app.

00:00:09.006 --> 00:00:12.868
The next call wakes a worker and waits for the answer.

00:00:12.868 --> 00:00:15.677
Here, one sleeping tool comes back with fifty-five.

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:17.798
Then the rush hits.

00:00:17.798 --> 00:00:19.621
We sent thirty calculations at once.

00:00:19.621 --> 00:00:22.962
The queue held the work while four workers shared the load.

00:00:23.875 --> 00:00:24.822
All thirty finished.

00:00:24.822 --> 00:00:30.190
The workers went back to zero, freeing capacity for the next thing your team wants to run.

00:00:31.125 --> 00:00:33.081
Pick a tool your agent already calls.

00:00:33.081 --> 00:00:35.596
Run the local demo and watch it wake up.

00:00:35.596 --> 00:00:36.714
Then let it sleep.
